   "source": [
    "# python series 012- sinusodial signals\n",
    "introduces the generation and visualisationof a sinusodial signal suing python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "52e97c97",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Mathematical model\n",
    "A sinusodial signal can be described by\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "s(t)=A\\sin(2\pi f t + \\phi)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where:\n",
    "\n",
    "-$A$ is the amplitude\n",
    "-$f$ is the frequency in Hz\n",
    "-$t$ is time in seconds\n",
    "-$\\phi$ is the phase"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6bd56001",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# python series 012- sinusodial signals\n",
    "introduces the generation and visualisationof a sinusodial signal suing python"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "a7c57309",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# create the time array\n",
    "t = np.linspace(0, 1, 1000)  # time from 0 to 1 second, 1000 points\n",
    "\n",
    "# create the sinusoidal signal\n",
    "f = 1  # frequency in Hz\n",
    "s = np.sin(2 * np.pi * f * t)  # sine wave\n",
    "\n",
    "#create the cosine signal\n",
    "c = np.cos(2 * np.pi * f * t)  # cosine wave\n",
    "\n",
    "#plot both signals\n",
    "plt.plot(t, s, label='Sine')\n",
    "plt.plot(t, c, label='Cosine')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add the title and labels\n",
    "plt.title('sinusoidal signal')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Time (s)')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Amplitude')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add a legend\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# add grid\n",
    "plt.grid(True)\n",
    "\n",
    "#save the plot as a PDF file\n",
    "plt.savefig('sinusoidal_signal.pdf', format='pdf')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# display the figure\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "306fc243",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def sinusoid(time, amplitude, frequency, phase):\n",
    "    x=amplitude * np.sin(2 * np.pi * frequency * time + phase)\n",
    "    return x"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "76436fc1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "s1 = sinusoid(t, 1, 1, 0)\n",
    "s2= sinusoid(t, 1, 2, 0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "952c761a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
